    "note": "31-38 m behind the stationary sedan the head deferred on 5 frames in 1-2 frame bursts (same noisy previous-source-speed input as the research replicates), and one 5-frame left signal (113.4-113.8 s) occurred while the sedan track was briefly unassociated; the planner's own pass votes cancelled it. None reached the six-vote commit. The head was not evaluated during the bus navigation merge (corridor merge) and associated the return-boulevard lead only after rejoin.",
    "margin": {
      "rule": "route_maneuvers.py lines 329-343: a discretionary pass commits when pass_votes reaches 6 and the source return is fresh (age 0); votes 1-5 show as signal_left; a source return older than 2 scans resets the count. After commit, a returned follow preference aborts while lateral > -0.35 m (motor queue early_outbound guard).",
      "native02": "4 consecutive votes (frames 1292-1295); ended when the head returned to follow.",
      "native03": "Reached 6 votes (frames 6266-6271). Commit was blocked only because the source return was 2 scans old on the 6th vote; the next frame was 3 scans old and reset the count. The head stayed on defer until frame 6274. Near miss: a fresh return at 6271 would have started a lane change.",
      "integrated_loop_01": "5 votes (frames 7777-7781) while the sedan track was unassociated (head inactive); ended by the frozen planner's compare_progress downgrade of pass to follow. One vote short.",
      "ground_truth": "Lead speed was 0.0 m/s on every deferral frame in native02 and native03 (reference-native.jsonl).",
      "assessment": "The head did not by itself reliably hold the car behind the stationary sedan in the 31-38 m window; outcomes there partly depended on scan timing and the base planner. Treat as an open defect before a featured capture."
